WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Hi, everyone.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Whitney Hodges: Hey, Carmen. Hello.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Marisa White: Okay.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Marisa White: Carmen, hey Whitney.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Whitney Hodges: Hey, Marissa. How's it going?

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Marisa White: Pretty good, pretty good. Um, I may be…

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Marisa White: off-camera. I'm kind of at that stage of always being horizontal with the… with the baby, so… um… but I am, uh… yeah, we're in the kind of final weeks here, so…

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Whitney Hodges: Yep. Mm-hmm.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, you're in the home stretch. It's so exciting.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Marisa White: Yes.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Whitney Hodges: Are you sleeping okay?

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Marisa White: Oh.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Marisa White: Yeah, I'm doing pretty good still. It's funny 'cause I keep being like, well, I'm almost at the end, so the sleep is only temporary, but then you're gonna get a different kind of no sleep. So I guess not really.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Exactly. I'm so excited for you guys.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Marisa White: Yeah. Thank you. And then Mike should be joining. He actually just reminded me about the meeting.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Marisa White: Um…

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Whitney Hodges: Well, we'll keep an eye on the waiting room or on him joining. How are things going on the DJ hybrid side of things?

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Marisa White: Very good, yeah, we've, um, we kind of have, uh, maybe it's just because everything is so busy right now, but it feels like there's been, like, an uptick in meetings scheduled, for sure. Um…

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.000
Whitney Hodges: I see.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Marisa White: And so that's been good. Um, we're booking some good meetings. Um, we're also… we've also kind of increased the price a bit, and it seems like that hasn't, um…

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Marisa White: you know, it's been a positive thing. It hasn't really, like, deterred.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Marisa White: the people reaching out, which is great. So yeah, I think it's all been pretty good so far.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Whitney Hodges: I love that. How much did you increase pricing?

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:02.000
Marisa White: So, um, we did… so, before, we were charging, I think, $4,000 as, like, the base…

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Marisa White: entry level package. So I increased that to 4,500. So everything kind of increased by 500. We also.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:28.000
Marisa White: added this idea of like the luxe DJ packages because it's sort of been a back and forth. So one of our saxophone players, you know, he has gotten really involved in, he kind of runs his own like saxophone.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Whitney Hodges: Hmm?

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:48.000
Marisa White: You can hire for him company, but we still work together with him. And so he was telling us like, you know, he's getting these really luxury weddings where he's charging like 2,500 just for himself, just for the saxophone, not for the DJ. And there definitely are some of those weddings that we're receiving, but we also are getting a lot.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Whitney Hodges: Got it.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.000
Whitney Hodges: Yes. Mm-hmm.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.000
Marisa White: that, you know.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:03:09.000
Marisa White: are choosing the DJ because of it being cost-effective. Um, so I don't want to lose those because it's still better to have a $4,500 wedding, you know, booked than none at all, right? Um, versus, like… and so we started adding, um, this idea of, like, the luxe packages to kind of hit.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.000
Whitney Hodges: Thank you.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Yes.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:17.000
Marisa White: You know, when you do have that more luxury budget, and you do want to have, like, an upgraded sound and light experience, um…

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:26.000
Marisa White: You know, maybe we could still capture those luxury clients without losing, kind of, the other clients that are really okay with our standard setup.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:44.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, that totally makes sense. Yeah, I love that. I think there's always, you know, a sweet spot in pricing, right, of where it's, like, you want to kind of get to the highest price point that you can without, like, sacrificing, like, the max volume that you want to do, and, like, there's this, like, balance, right? Because if it…

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:50.000
Whitney Hodges: Gets to a point where it's priced even just a little too high, then it can end up being something where you're just…

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.000
Whitney Hodges: Ultimately, not booking as much as you want to be, you know?

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.000
Marisa White: Yeah, exactly.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:08.000
Marisa White: you know, and you also don't want to miss the luxury clients where, like, they… they're not… like, they might not even look at us if we're, like… I mean, that would be in my head, too, like, if you… you're looking at a vendor who's $2,000 versus.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:13.000
Marisa White: You kind of know you're getting a different product at those two price points, so…

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.000
Whitney Hodges: Exactly. Yeah. Okay. Awesome.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.000
